{"description":"Produce and publish the two build variants across the fleet's targets, and the coordinator container image.\n\nDefault build — pure Go, fully static, no C toolchain: linux/amd64, linux/arm64, linux/arm, darwin/arm64, darwin/amd64, windows/amd64.\n\nAudio build — `voice` tag, CGO via zig cc: linux/amd64, linux/arm64, darwin/arm64.\n\nThe two-variant split is what makes walkie/adr:002-runtime-stack's 'degrade rather than fail' promise real rather than aspirational, so this item is what verifies that promise.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. Every default-build target is produced by continuous integration with no C toolchain in the build environment.\n2. A default-build binary is verified to be statically linked and free of CGO.\n3. Every audio-build target is produced using zig cc, without a per-target sysroot.\n4. Builds are reproducible: the same commit produces identical artifacts.\n5. The coordinator image runs the tsnet-based coordinator without host networking.\n6. Release artifacts carry checksums. Signing is deferred to the phase 4 auto-update work and that deferral is recorded, not silently skipped.\n7. Both variants are smoke-tested on a real fleet ARM device before release, not only in emulation."}